  "s2": "S2 initialises from the weakened givens (no derived parent eliminations); it shortens accepted tests only; performance scope: the minimal early-exit prototype, the planned initial-state cache is not implemented",
  "interpretations": [
    "PhaseA runs the bounded native DFS uniqueness count after EVERY refused floor test (floor solve genuinely stuck), at every rung; a proved second solution rejects the group permanently (never retested at a later rung), an unknown or capped count keeps the entry with proof \"unknown\"",
    "A ladder keeps, per group, only the LAST rung's eligible failure as the phaseB entry (new discovery ordinal); earlier rungs stay diagnostics; an entry is dropped when its group is later removed or proved ambiguous",
    "The S2 signal is not raised when the grid is complete at that step: the solve finishes and is a complete proof",
